Package: analyticgrimu
Title: Granularity Testing for Mann-Whitney U-Test Reported Results
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ian", "Hussey", , "ian.hussey@unibe.ch", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8906-7559"))
  )
Description: Forensic meta-science tools for checking whether reported
    Mann-Whitney U test results are mathematically possible. Published U
    statistics and p-values are rounded, so a reported value is consistent
    only if some attainable exact value falls within its rounding window.
    Given the two group sizes, the package enumerates every U statistic the
    test can produce and the p-values it implies under the reporting
    conventions of common software (exact doubled-tail, 'SPSS' Exact /
    'StatXact' deviation-from-mean, mid-p, and tie-corrected asymptotic
    approximations), then asks whether the reported statistic, p-value, and
    their pairing could have arisen together. When none can, the reported
    result is flagged 'inconsistent'. This implements the GRIM-U granularity
    test of Heathers and Grimes (2025)
    <https://medicalevidenceproject.org/grim-u-observation-establish-impossible-p-values-ranked-tests/>,
    extending the GRIM family of consistency tests to ranked tests. The
    package also reports the granularity (p-value saturation) of a design
    and visualises the attainable p-value space.
